Theorem TF-13: capture_state_update monotonicity (OxCaml LAM pattern, both branches)

  Preconditions:
    - capture_state_update(current, closure_state) per Annex E §AIMS TF-13
      OxCaml LAM (Locality-And-Multiplicity) pattern is the SSOT for
      captured-arg backward state mutation
    - Two branches per closure cardinality:
        Branch 1 (closure cardinality <= Once):
          consumption := seq_add(current.consumption, Affine)
          cardinality := seq_add(current.cardinality, Once)
          locality := max(current.locality, closure_state.locality)
        Branch 2 (closure cardinality > Once, i.e., Many):
          consumption := Unrestricted
          cardinality := Many
          locality := max(current.locality, closure_state.locality)
    - Access promotion clause (cross-cuts both branches):
        closure_state.locality >= HeapEscaping implies access := Owned
      Rationale (per Annex E §AIMS TF-13 + CN-8 interaction): Borrowed
      captures whose closure lifetime escapes the defining scope would
      outlive their source — CN-8 clamps Borrowed locality to FunctionLocal
      while the closure escapes; promoting Access to Owned establishes the
      logical ownership extension at the capture site. A physical executor
      chooses how to realize that extension.
    - L-6 monotonicity: capture_state_update SHALL be monotone in
      closure_state for fixed current (per Annex E §AIMS TF-13 statement
      "SHALL be monotone per L-6")
    - Carriers (per §1.2 Consumption, §1.3 Cardinality, §1.5 Locality):
        Consumption: Dead < Linear < Affine < Unrestricted
        Cardinality: Absent < Once < Many
        Locality: BlockLocal < FunctionLocal < ArgEscaping < HeapEscaping
                     < Unknown

  Soundness property:
    Forall current, closure_state in AimsState. Forall closure_card in
    {Once, Many} (the two branches of the §3 TF-13 case split).
      capture_state_update(current, closure_state, closure_card) produces
      output per the branch above
    AND closure_state.locality1 <=_L closure_state.locality2 implies
        capture_state_update(c, s1, k).locality <=_L
        capture_state_update(c, s2, k).locality (L-6 layer (b) per
        argument locality)
    AND closure_state.locality1 >= HeapEscaping implies output.access = Owned
    AND output is monotone componentwise in closure_state across the lattice.

  Proof obligation:
    Three-part discharge:
      (a) Branch-1 enumeration (closure_card <= Once) — verify the
          consumption / cardinality / locality update over a representative
          enumeration of (current, closure_state) pairs; verify monotone in
          closure_state.
      (b) Branch-2 enumeration (closure_card > Once) — verify constant
          assignment (consumption := Unrestricted, cardinality := Many) +
          locality := max; verify monotone in closure_state.
      (c) Access promotion clause enumeration — for each closure_state with
          locality >= HeapEscaping, verify output.access = Owned regardless
          of current.access.

    Part (a) — branch-1 (closure_card <= Once):
      Pick representative (current, closure_state) pairs and verify each
      output component matches the spec:
        consumption := seq_add(current.consumption, Affine)
        cardinality := seq_add(current.cardinality, Once)
        locality := max(current.locality, closure_state.locality)
      The seq_add definitions are inherited from TF-11.proof Parts (b) + (c)
      (Consumption + Cardinality matrices). Monotonicity in closure_state:
      since locality is max(current, closure_state.locality), it is monotone
      in closure_state.locality by monotonicity of max over a chain (§1.5).
      Consumption and cardinality are independent of closure_state under
      this branch — trivially monotone.

    Part (b) — branch-2 (closure_card > Once):
      The constants Unrestricted (consumption) and Many (cardinality) are
      lattice-TOP for their carriers; monotonicity holds vacuously (constant
      output). Locality update = max(current.locality, closure_state.locality)
      is monotone in closure_state.locality as in part (a).

    Part (c) — Access promotion clause:
      Per Annex E §AIMS TF-13 + CN-8: closure_state.locality >=
      HeapEscaping implies output.access := Owned (regardless of current.access).
      Verified by enumerating closure_state.locality over LOCALITY_CARRIER
      and checking:
        closure_state.locality in {BlockLocal, FunctionLocal, ArgEscaping}:
          output.access := current.access (no promotion)
        closure_state.locality in {HeapEscaping, Unknown}:
          output.access := Owned (promoted)
      Negative witness: if Access promotion did NOT fire on HeapEscaping,
      Borrowed-locality clamping by CN-8 (clamps to FunctionLocal) would
      end the captured variable's lifetime with its FunctionLocal source
      even though the escaping closure still references it. Owned extends
      the logical ownership lifetime to the escaping closure lifetime.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) over closure_state per
        section_04::verify_tf13_capture_state_update_monotone)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — 2-branch (closure_card) split + Access
        promotion enumeration over LOCALITY_CARRIER per
        section_04::verify_tf13_capture_state_update_monotone)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; max + seq_add monotone per
        L-6 layer (a))
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-13 does NOT call
        refine())

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-13 via 2-branch enumeration + monotonicity over closure_state + Access promotion enumeration on locality >= HeapEscaping
